=== F. FINRA 5130: a new issue is an equity IPO, not every offering ===
a member may not sell a new issue to an account in which a restricted person has a beneficial interest, except as the rule permits
new issue means an initial public offering of an equity security, made pursuant to a registration statement or offering circular
the offering-price first-day return is not a fill every account could have earned
  equity IPO: 5130 new issue? True
  follow-on / additional offering of already-public stock: 5130 new issue? False
  preferred offering: in the official shall-not-include list? True
  convertible offering: in the official shall-not-include list? True
  ordinary shares or Form F-6 ADRs with a pre-existing market outside the United States: in the official shall-not-include list? True
